                <pb facs="0407" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1088: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-24T17:00:00-04:32">July 24, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>51. I have been officially informed by the Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    that yesterday the final act in accordance with the Washington agreement was
                    signed and that Forts Boquerón and Vanguardia were returned in the presence of
                    Uruguayan officers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
